 "stop": "3 quatrains",
 "poem": "And, as a king mine father,\nI shall stand in the blast of heaven's power\nAnd the future of my life. But again\nThe day breaks: and after day,\nThe darkness is like to darkness\nOf old age; I search not why that morning\nShall bring its summer down at all again;\nAnd yet ere it make me weary still\nMy task must be done, and again\nI fear; I fear no perhaps\nThat that golden hour come too early\nTo see what I am but going down,",
